WEBVTT

00:00:08.830 --> 00:00:12.370
The Imber has picked up the guide beacon.
It is now on course.

00:00:12.660 --> 00:00:16.200
Touchdown in 10 seconds.
Nine, eight, seven,

00:00:16.200 --> 00:00:18.250
six, five,

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:22.200
four, three, two, one.

00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:27.750
Touchdown confirmed.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:31.750
Well done.

00:00:32.700 --> 00:00:34.410
That was good work.

00:00:34.410 --> 00:00:36.040
Thank you very much.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:37.620
Yes.

00:00:37.620 --> 00:00:40.040
And Miss Amami, your engagement
of the target was perfect.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:46.660
It looks like we can leave control
of the Imber to Yukiho now.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.700
Yes. I have nothing more to teach her.

00:00:50.870 --> 00:00:52.290
That's not true.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.040
How modest you are!

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.540
Yukiho Hagiwara.

00:00:56.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Sir!

00:00:57.160 --> 00:01:01.160
I formally request you become
the Imber's operator.

00:01:02.250 --> 00:01:03.160
Sir!

00:01:03.410 --> 00:01:05.410
Congratulations, Yukiho.

00:01:05.410 --> 00:01:06.910
Good luck.

00:01:08.200 --> 00:01:10.950
The birth of a rookie duo, yes?

00:01:12.750 --> 00:01:14.410
Good job, Yukiho!

00:01:14.410 --> 00:01:15.870
You too, Haruka!

00:01:19.660 --> 00:01:21.830
We did it, Imber.

00:01:32.870 --> 00:01:35.540
Gonna change, gonna change!

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:39.040
Gotta change, gonna change!

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:45.290
Huh? Is swapping the bones out a
"change"? What do you think, Chihaya?

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.540
Go on, Karasu.

00:01:50.830 --> 00:01:54.410
This frame was designed with increased
lightness rather than durability in mind.

00:01:54.410 --> 00:01:57.000
Hey! Don't ignore me!
This frame was designed with increased
lightness rather than durability in mind.

00:01:57.790 --> 00:02:02.120
I ask that you not disappoint Mother,
who has authorized its use.

00:02:02.620 --> 00:02:04.330
I understand, Karasu.

00:02:04.870 --> 00:02:09.000
The Imber was originally mine.
I WILL get it back.

00:02:09.450 --> 00:02:11.540
Tell that to Mother.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.790
S.O.S. kikoeta

00:02:16.790 --> 00:02:21.750
Yatto anata ni kikoeta?

00:02:35.290 --> 00:02:37.700
Kakko kawaiku ne

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:41.250
Fujun, junsui, dotchi no character?

00:02:41.250 --> 00:02:44.080
Onaji na no kashira

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:46.620
Love beat ga sokudo zenkai

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:51.620
Kizuita, kore wa tokubetsu na mission... Wakatta

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.040
Honki misechau yo, kanaechau kara

00:02:58.040 --> 00:03:01.910
Sora o tsukinuketa sekai de

00:03:02.870 --> 00:03:08.870
Fushigi na omoi kanjita yo, shunkan de suki!

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:13.910
Egao de katsu desho, yappa egao wa tadashii no

00:03:13.910 --> 00:03:17.250
Egao de katsu desho, yappa egao wa tadashii no

00:03:17.250 --> 00:03:22.830
Naiteta chiisa na watashi ga tachimukau

00:03:22.830 --> 00:03:25.160
Nandaro doki doki, chotto teate ga hitsuyou ne

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.450
Nandaro doki doki, chotto teate ga hitsuyou ne

00:03:28.450 --> 00:03:36.540
Binetsu na kibun wa anata no sei kamo, S.O.S.!

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:50.080
And so, now that Yukiho has become
my operat... I mean, my manager,

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:54.040
it's like I'm getting along better
with that kid, too.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:54.450
Altitude: 20,000 Meters

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:57.620
You mean, that kid from your
club activities you mentioned before?

00:03:57.830 --> 00:04:02.870
Yeah. It's like, if we're together,
I can do anything. Or something.

00:04:03.120 --> 00:04:07.160
Say, Haruka, is this kid
from your club a boy?

00:04:07.330 --> 00:04:09.200
Yeah. Probably.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:10.660
Probably?

00:04:10.660 --> 00:04:13.450
That's not what I meant! He's a boy, yeah!

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:15.830
Is he tall? Is he cool?

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:21.120
He's REALLY tall. I don't know
if he's "cool," though.

00:04:21.540 --> 00:04:26.160
Ah! In missio...
In sports meets, he's kinda cool.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:28.790
Oh. I get it.

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:31.120
Haruka. You're smitten, huh?

00:04:31.910 --> 00:04:37.200
I wanna meet him. I'll find out for sure
if he's good to be your boyfriend!

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:40.000
Boyfriend?! You've got it wrong!

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.080
See ya!

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:44.660
I said you're wrong! Yayoi! Yayoi!

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.750
Jeez. That's not it at all.

00:04:58.500 --> 00:05:04.080
Still... We can have
a little adventure. Right?

00:05:06.160 --> 00:05:11.120
Thus, you will both be studying
practical iDOL maintenance today.

00:05:11.500 --> 00:05:15.200
Well, sometimes it's good
to get yourself dirty with oil.

00:05:17.250 --> 00:05:19.790
And after I'd gotten all dressed up...

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.750
What's the matter?

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:23.370
Nothing at all!

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:28.830
Okay, Miss Ribbon, just what
do you think that's doing?

00:05:28.830 --> 00:05:33.410
Um... an X-ray?

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:38.450
Close. It's an ultrasound-based
frame stress test.

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:40.160
Stress?

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:43.790
A big humanoid frame like
that is inherently problematic.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.290
It shouldn't even be able to stand upright.

00:05:47.450 --> 00:05:49.290
Then... The Imber is...

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:51.160
It's because of inertial control.

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.500
Bingo!

00:05:52.500 --> 00:05:57.870
A strange technology, a super outrageous
feat of strength only possible for iDOLs.

00:05:58.250 --> 00:06:02.910
Inertial control lets these
giant "kids" fly and even leap.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:06.250
Still, it pushes them beyond their limits,

00:06:06.250 --> 00:06:10.120
and when they destroy Drops,
they of course incur damage.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.950
So after every sortie,
we inspect them like this.

00:06:17.290 --> 00:06:22.500
If accumulated frame damage reaches
a certain point, we can remove-

00:06:22.500 --> 00:06:24.540
It's too soon for C Maintenance, isn't it?!

00:06:24.830 --> 00:06:28.500
Nebula's frame has already been
replaced twice in the last six months!

00:06:28.540 --> 00:06:31.000
You have no right to interfere, Minase.

00:06:31.200 --> 00:06:33.700
But, it's too much!

00:06:35.700 --> 00:06:41.620
Current accumulated stress is 33.42. The
rules say we trade out once it reaches 40,

00:06:41.620 --> 00:06:44.080
and there's a chance it'll cross
that in the next sortie.

00:06:44.450 --> 00:06:48.080
In that case, a Master can request
C Maintenance based on her judgment.

00:06:48.250 --> 00:06:51.330
A tool must always be in top condition.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.580
"Tool"? Makoto, why you...!

00:06:55.120 --> 00:06:56.830
Don't do it, Iori.

00:06:57.700 --> 00:06:58.910
That's...

00:06:59.660 --> 00:07:01.540
I don't think that's right.

00:07:09.000 --> 00:07:13.580
Say, Chihaya. We can give it
our all for real, right?

00:07:13.700 --> 00:07:14.790
Of course.

00:07:20.330 --> 00:07:21.660
I look forward to it.

00:07:26.660 --> 00:07:28.660
Plan on picking a fight again?

00:07:29.620 --> 00:07:36.700
No, it's not like that. But I think iDOLs
really do have something like a mind.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:40.160
Amami. You, too?

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:44.660
If you keep thinking like that,
you'll make a big mistake...

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.950
One you can't take back.

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:52.290
That's not true! Just today,
I was able to take out a Drop on my own!

00:07:52.450 --> 00:07:56.290
Of that scale, yes. But what if
a greater one comes along?

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:00.870
I-Imber and I can handle
anything that comes up!

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:04.290
We've received a flash from HQ!

00:08:04.290 --> 00:08:06.330
All pilots, stand by to deploy!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.910
I repeat, all pilots, stand by to deploy!

00:08:07.910 --> 00:08:09.330
We launch in three minutes!
I repeat, all pilots, stand by to deploy!

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:10.250
Ma'am!

00:08:10.250 --> 00:08:11.370
All staff of Prometheus 1 and Prometheus 2,

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.750
I'm goin' too, Makoto.
All staff of Prometheus 1 and Prometheus 2,

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:13.620
Sorry, but we'll get to
the frame exchange later.
All staff of Prometheus 1 and Prometheus 2,

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:15.200
Sorry, but we'll get to
the frame exchange later.
begin preparations to sortie!

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:16.660
Guess it can't be helped.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:22.580
I don't want you to forget what I've said.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:28.830
Both at about the same time?

00:08:28.830 --> 00:08:31.250
Yes. With a sizeable
distance between them.

00:08:33.370 --> 00:08:36.450
Chief, can Miss Amami do it on her own?

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:39.830
I'm sure she'll be fine.
She seems plenty motivated.

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:41.370
Ow...

00:08:47.620 --> 00:08:48.500
Okay!

00:08:48.500 --> 00:08:52.620
In that case, it's good we've adopted
a two-unit procedure.

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:53.910
A second transmission from HQ.

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.120
Target Alpha and Target Bravo
have been confirmed as Lemons.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:08:59.910
Receiving orders to sortie!

00:09:00.250 --> 00:09:03.910
Yukiho. Naze. Are your
Idolmasters on standby?

00:09:04.370 --> 00:09:05.950
She'll be onstage shortly.

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.910
Yukiho?

00:09:06.910 --> 00:09:08.410
S-same here!

00:09:17.870 --> 00:09:20.540
Prometheus 1 and 2, standing by!

00:09:21.000 --> 00:09:22.910
Systems are all green.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:24.750
Inform the Ministry of Transport.

00:09:24.750 --> 00:09:27.120
Sir. Securing Channels 9 and 17.

00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:29.660
Nebula and Imber, deploy!

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:31.660
Nebula, deploy!

00:09:35.620 --> 00:09:39.750
Let's do our best, Imber. We can do it.

00:09:58.700 --> 00:10:00.750
Imber, deploy!

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:17.660
There's one konpeito,
there are two konpeito...

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:25.450
Targets Alpha and Bravo
are proceeding along planned orbits.

00:10:25.620 --> 00:10:28.620
The Nebula has reached airspace
above the Pacific Ocean.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.250
It is 60 seconds to live point.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.700
The Imber is above the Indian Ocean.
80 seconds to point.

00:10:34.330 --> 00:10:37.040
Makoto, you should be able
to visually confirm.

00:10:37.080 --> 00:10:38.450
I'm trying.

00:10:38.660 --> 00:10:40.790
Haruka, can you see it?

00:10:44.040 --> 00:10:45.700
I'm looking, but...

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.500
Trajectory is confirmed.

00:10:51.500 --> 00:10:54.290
According to the data, it should
have long been visible.

00:10:56.040 --> 00:10:57.080
Naraba.

00:10:57.330 --> 00:11:00.330
I'm now comparing with
observation data from each branch.

00:11:03.250 --> 00:11:05.410
The Drops disappeared!

00:11:06.540 --> 00:11:11.290
More, more, eat more. Konpeito!

00:11:13.040 --> 00:11:15.450
Targets Charlie and Delta have appeared.

00:11:15.450 --> 00:11:18.000
They're confirmed as Lemons!
We have the order to deploy!

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:23.500
Echo and Foxtrot have appeared!
Status: Lemon. We have orders to deploy!

00:11:23.620 --> 00:11:25.370
Just what is going on?

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:28.160
Charlie and Delta have disappeared.

00:11:28.160 --> 00:11:28.910
Now, Golf and Hotel have appeared.

00:11:28.910 --> 00:11:30.450
It's a mistake, right? Lemon Drops
can't suddenly disappear, can they?!
Now, Golf and Hotel have appeared.

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:33.290
It's a mistake, right? Lemon Drops
can't suddenly disappear, can they?!

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:34.700
Naraba!

00:11:34.910 --> 00:11:35.830
Ma'am?

00:11:35.830 --> 00:11:40.660
Run a self-diagnostic on
the base's mainframe. Check all circuits.

00:11:41.000 --> 00:11:41.750
Understood!

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:42.870
Sir.

00:11:43.370 --> 00:11:44.250
This is...

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:46.000
Don't tell me...!

00:11:49.830 --> 00:11:53.160
The base's systems have been hacked?!

00:11:55.250 --> 00:11:57.500
Check complete. There are no errors.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:12:00.330
If it's a cracker, it must be Wizard class.

00:12:00.500 --> 00:12:03.410
But, ma'am! How could they
penetrate the base's defenses?

00:12:03.620 --> 00:12:05.870
Look at what's right in front of you.

00:12:06.410 --> 00:12:08.040
What shall we do, sir?

00:12:08.370 --> 00:12:11.950
Even if the information may be spurious,

00:12:11.950 --> 00:12:16.540
if we receive Drop info from HQ,
we cannot ignore it.

00:12:17.160 --> 00:12:18.250
Miss Kikuchi.

00:12:18.910 --> 00:12:20.040
Miss Amami.

00:12:20.200 --> 00:12:22.080
Um, it's all right.

00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.040
I'll do it!

00:12:23.040 --> 00:12:24.290
Please do.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:25.500
Sir.

00:12:25.660 --> 00:12:27.330
Permission to leave the command room.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:29.040
I shall seek a counter-method.

00:12:29.040 --> 00:12:30.290
Please do.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:32.750
Let's do our best, Imber.
We have to protect everyone!

00:12:32.750 --> 00:12:34.450
Let's do our best, Imber.
We have to protect everyone!
Foxtrot has disappeared!

00:12:34.450 --> 00:12:35.950
Let's do our best, Imber.
We have to protect everyone!
And now India and Kilo have appeared!

00:12:36.450 --> 00:12:37.370
Understood!

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:41.160
Lima and Mike have appeared!

00:12:41.410 --> 00:12:42.910
I can't confirm Lima.

00:12:43.410 --> 00:12:44.620
Mike is clear.

00:12:44.870 --> 00:12:46.040
Next is November.

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:47.040
Not there!

00:12:47.200 --> 00:12:47.950
Oscar!

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:48.950
Clear.

00:12:49.160 --> 00:12:50.040
Papa!

00:12:50.040 --> 00:12:50.950
Not there!

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:51.700
Quebec!

00:12:51.700 --> 00:12:52.290
Clear!

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:53.700
Is this a nightmare?

00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:59.160
Oh my, things are heating up.

00:12:59.790 --> 00:13:01.870
Almost, maybe?

00:13:07.700 --> 00:13:08.620
Makoto?

00:13:08.620 --> 00:13:09.910
No problem. What's next?

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:22.950
Jeez.

00:13:22.950 --> 00:13:24.950
I'm soaked to my panties.

00:13:25.410 --> 00:13:26.620
Haruka!

00:13:26.620 --> 00:13:29.450
It's all right. I'm a long way from fin-

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.620
Hyaa!

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:35.500
Huh? Yukiho?

00:13:36.620 --> 00:13:37.830
Wh-what?

00:13:37.830 --> 00:13:38.750
What happened?!

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:40.370
I lost Haruka's transmission!

00:13:40.660 --> 00:13:42.410
The Nebula's transmission cut off, too.

00:13:42.660 --> 00:13:44.370
The transponder isn't responding!

00:13:45.290 --> 00:13:46.500
What happened?

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:48.330
This has never happened before.

00:14:05.370 --> 00:14:08.870
We... can do it, right?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:10.500
Imber!

00:14:24.160 --> 00:14:25.450
Go!

00:14:36.410 --> 00:14:37.410
We did it!

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:57.910
What is going on?!

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.790
Where are the Imber and the Nebula?!

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:01.660
We can't restore transmission!

00:15:01.660 --> 00:15:03.410
The radar is still on white out.

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.910
System repeat!

00:15:05.120 --> 00:15:06.790
It's no good! I can't raise them!

00:15:06.790 --> 00:15:07.870
What's going on?

00:15:08.500 --> 00:15:09.790
Haruka...

00:15:12.620 --> 00:15:14.080
A falling star?

00:15:37.790 --> 00:15:39.700
What was that?

00:15:48.290 --> 00:15:49.450
We're okay?

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:04.790
What's goin' on?

00:16:09.370 --> 00:16:11.330
What? What is this?

00:16:18.120 --> 00:16:19.290
That's...

00:16:22.370 --> 00:16:23.450
From before!

00:16:58.410 --> 00:17:01.830
Yes, yes, Chihaya! Go, go, Nubilum!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:06.950
Huh? Who? Who is interfering?!

00:17:08.700 --> 00:17:12.080
We wooooon't be beaten!

00:17:13.870 --> 00:17:17.410
You will give it back. That robot is MINE.

00:17:26.830 --> 00:17:30.500
If you keep thinking like that,
you'll make a big mistake...

00:17:30.830 --> 00:17:32.450
One you can't take back.

00:17:32.830 --> 00:17:36.410
I-Imber and I can handle anything
that comes up!

00:17:38.370 --> 00:17:41.700
I can't. If I run away, everyone will...

00:17:42.790 --> 00:17:47.950
It's all right. We're all right, right?

00:17:47.950 --> 00:17:49.000
Imber!

00:17:53.950 --> 00:17:54.950
We can...

00:17:59.410 --> 00:18:00.370
...do it!

00:18:20.290 --> 00:18:21.250
It's still not restored?

00:18:21.250 --> 00:18:22.250
Nebula! Respond!
It's still not restored?

00:18:22.250 --> 00:18:23.080
Nebula! Respond!
Still trying!

00:18:23.080 --> 00:18:24.160
Haruka! Haruka!
Still trying!

00:18:24.330 --> 00:18:27.120
Makoto! Respond! What's going on?!

00:18:27.120 --> 00:18:28.330
It was cancelled!
Makoto! Respond! What's going on?!

00:18:28.330 --> 00:18:30.000
Our requests aren't going through.
Makoto! Respond! What's going on?!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.290
Our requests aren't going through.

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:31.290
Idiot Ribbon!

00:18:31.370 --> 00:18:32.620
We're being circumvented by the enemy's
logic barrier. We can't contact MSA!

00:18:32.620 --> 00:18:34.660
Chief, nothing yet?
We're being circumvented by the enemy's
logic barrier. We can't contact MSA!

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:45.040
SO HOT!

00:18:47.870 --> 00:18:49.910
All systems are restored!

00:18:49.910 --> 00:18:50.830
What's going on?

00:18:51.540 --> 00:18:55.750
We can ascertain the reasons later.
Confirm the Imber and Nebula's status!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:58.080
Makoto! Makoto? You okay?

00:18:58.250 --> 00:19:02.200
Yeah. I've linked with the American branch
and am standing guard in orbit.

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:03.080
It's all clear.

00:19:03.330 --> 00:19:05.080
Understood. Next-

00:19:05.080 --> 00:19:07.160
Haruka! Haruka!

00:19:07.750 --> 00:19:08.910
Respond!

00:19:09.200 --> 00:19:10.580
Haruka!

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:13.450
Haruka is... Lines are back up, and yet...!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:17.370
Calm down, Yukiho.
Confirm her coordinates.

00:19:17.370 --> 00:19:18.370
Ma'am.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:22.580
Prometheus 1's current coordinates
are Alpha 135, Sigma 53?

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.080
Off the coast of the Sea of Japan?

00:19:24.080 --> 00:19:24.910
When did she return to shore?

00:19:24.910 --> 00:19:26.040
Any usable cameras?
When did she return to shore?

00:19:26.290 --> 00:19:28.450
Got a hit on a lighthouse
surveillance monitor!

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:29.950
Retrieving feed...

00:19:37.500 --> 00:19:39.500
It can't be! Not that!

00:19:44.450 --> 00:19:45.580
No!

00:19:46.290 --> 00:19:48.080
Haruka! Answer us!

00:19:48.370 --> 00:19:49.830
Come in, dammit!

00:19:50.370 --> 00:19:51.910
You Idiot Ribbon!

00:19:53.790 --> 00:19:59.080
Pilot status... Pulse rate, blood pressure
and body temperature are all decreasing!

00:19:59.250 --> 00:20:03.750
Detecting abnormal levels in all hormones.
She could be unconscious and bleeding.

00:20:03.750 --> 00:20:06.290
Frame stress is at the breaking point!

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:10.450
All Imber systems are down.
Inertial control is not responding.

00:20:10.790 --> 00:20:13.000
At this point, all attacks
will be absorbed directly!

00:20:15.540 --> 00:20:18.540
What a... What a terrible turn of events.

00:20:18.830 --> 00:20:19.700
Makoto!

00:20:20.120 --> 00:20:21.290
I know.

00:20:27.040 --> 00:20:30.910
Frame stress is at 58.
We're about at our limit, too.

00:20:32.120 --> 00:20:35.580
Chihaya! Someone interfered
and I had to call it quits!

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.200
I was really enjoying that bath!

00:20:43.330 --> 00:20:44.410
What the...?

00:20:45.410 --> 00:20:48.580
The Nubilum is airborne.
It's picking up speed!

00:20:48.750 --> 00:20:50.410
Altitude: 5,000... 10,000....

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:51.540
She wants to take it with her?
Altitude: 5,000... 10,000....

00:20:51.540 --> 00:20:53.160
Then why go straight up?

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:54.120
Oh, no!

00:20:56.620 --> 00:21:01.040
Imber. Soon, I will release you
from that Master.

00:21:01.700 --> 00:21:03.620
She plans to drop the Imber?

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:07.750
With the inertial controls not working,
Haruka will be...!

00:21:07.950 --> 00:21:09.830
She'd take the whole impact of her fall!

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:13.290
Altitude: 20,000 meters.
The Nubilum has ceased to climb.

00:21:14.700 --> 00:21:15.870
Idiot Ribbon!

00:21:48.700 --> 00:21:50.620
Haruka!

00:21:56.330 --> 00:22:05.250
Toki o wataru seija no you ni

00:22:05.250 --> 00:22:14.250
Donna kodoku ni naite ita no?

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:23.120
Haruka tooi hoshi o tsunagi

00:22:23.120 --> 00:22:31.660
Ne, omoi o egaku wa, sora o miagete

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:43.080
Dear boy, itsumo kokoro ni anata o sagaseba

00:22:43.080 --> 00:22:52.080
Ah, dakishimeru hodo ni tsuyoi hikari o hanatsu no

00:22:52.080 --> 00:23:01.000
Mabataku kidou ga futari no mejirushi

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:12.620
Ima doko de mite ite mo truth kanjitete

00:23:26.000 --> 00:23:41.040
Preview
I'm Home. Welcome Back.

00:23:27.290 --> 00:23:31.000
Haruka, what do you like about penguins?

00:23:31.000 --> 00:23:32.290
Well, of course...

00:23:32.290 --> 00:23:33.330
Of course?

00:23:33.330 --> 00:23:37.870
Even in harshest winters,
the males will warm the eggs all alone!

00:23:37.870 --> 00:23:39.160
That's why?
